In article <1990Jan9.160231.3726@cs.rochester.edu> raman@cs.rochester.edu (Rajeev Raman) writes:
>How about this: a ring, when worn sufficiently long, will have an adverse
>permanent effect. 
>
...
>
>This idea will need further work: 1) to make sure it makes a difference,
>and 2) to avoid loopholes that might cause it to become easier, by `cheating'.
>It has the advantage of being `natural' to some degree, and maybe will
>be relatively easy to code up.

Seems like it would not be easy to code up without making the game easier.

Certainly if a +1 ring of gain strength were to affect its wearer, then
a -1 ring should do the same.  And it would be a pain to suddenly collapse
under your load if the gained strength were to slowly wear off.

Another thing which could happen is that a +3 ring would give a +6 when worn,
leading to an issue of charges in a ring.  Can the lost strength be regained
through a restore strength potion, and if so, what happens with the '+6' ring?

Actually, come to think of it, I don't see how 'natural' this method is in
general.  Except for gaunlets of power, strength aids only enhance normal
strength, and most of the time (at least for me) there is more than enough
things to carry to use all the strength I can get.  Similarly, just because
I'm more dextrous does not mean I'm not going to try as hard as I can to 
dodge some attack.

I could see this implemented for fire and cold resistance, but to me it
would be similar to having your strength go up because you're carrying a
lot of stuff all the time, or down because of resting and praying to
gods :-), and I don't see this happening in the near future.

